The built site includes image encoders from jSquash (https://github.com/jamsinclair/jSquash),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, which are compiled from libwebp (BSD-3-Clause),
libavif and libaom (BSD-2-Clause) and MozJPEG (IJG, BSD-3-Clause and zlib licenses). Their license
files are copied next to the binaries in wasm/. Licenses of the other bundled packages are listed in
3rdpartylicenses.txt of the built site.

To convert HEIC and HEIF photos in browsers that cannot decode them, the built site loads libheif
(https://github.com/strukturag/libheif, with libde265), built for the web by libheif-js
(https://github.com/catdad-experiments/libheif-js) and licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
License, version 3. It is kept as separate files in heif/ (libheif.js, libheif.wasm), with its
license in heif/LICENSE.libheif.txt, and is loaded only when such a photo is added; it can be
replaced with another build of the same library.
